From: mohitt31 <mohitprajapati3112@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 02:34:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix: include <sys/time.h> for struct timeval in the proxy

Proxy/Tools.h declares

    auto sec(struct timeval start, struct timeval end) -> double;

but only includes <ctime>. struct timeval comes from <sys/time.h>; glibc
happens to pull it in transitively via <ctime>, so this builds on Linux,
but on macOS it does not and Tools.cpp fails with

    error: variable has incomplete type 'struct timeval'

Runner.cpp already includes <sys/time.h> explicitly, which is why only
Tools.cpp breaks. Include it in the header instead, so the header is
self-contained for anyone declaring or calling sec().
Contains AI-generated content. (model: Opus 5)
---
 src/Proxy/Tools.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/Proxy/Tools.h b/src/Proxy/Tools.h
index cf190815..0dd8ffc0 100644
--- a/src/Proxy/Tools.h
+++ b/src/Proxy/Tools.h
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #define SEISSOL_SRC_PROXY_TOOLS_H_
 
 #include <ctime>
+#include <sys/time.h>
 
 auto derive_cycles_from_time(double time) -> double;
 
